<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>TEI Simler, with what its rendering needs declared</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <p>Part of the ODD Rendering Compiler proof of concept.</p>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>Changes two elements of tei_simler.odd, which stays as Simler Digital has it.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <p>What a page renders is the ODD's to say, and two things in Simler's rendering are not yet
        in its ODD: the preview's code holds them. So this ODD chains to it (<att>source</att> on
        <gi>schemaSpec</gi>) and declares them, with the models of <gi>lb</gi> and <gi>note</gi>
        otherwise copied; a test holds the copies to the original. Once the Simler ODD says the
        same, this file goes.</p>
      <schemaSpec ident="tei_simler_render" start="TEI" source="tei_simler.odd">
        <elementSpec ident="lb" mode="change">
          <!-- added: the param join, the characters a joined line's text may end in, which go -->
          <model cssClass="lb-hyphen" predicate="@break='no' and matches(preceding-sibling::node()[normalize-space()][1], '[-¬⸗&#xAD;&#x2010;&#x2011;]\s*$')" behaviour="break">
            <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
            <param name="label" value="'-'"/>
            <param name="join" value="'-¬⸗&#xAD;&#x2010;&#x2011;'"/>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="lb-hyphen-supplied" predicate="@break='no'" behaviour="break">
            <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
            <param name="label" value="'-'"/>
            <param name="join" value="'-¬⸗&#xAD;&#x2010;&#x2011;'"/>
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <modelSequence>
            <model behaviour="break">
              <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
            </model>
            <!-- the line end is a word boundary, except a forme work line's: the text's own line
                 end before it already is one, and a word joined across the page goes on after it -->
            <model behaviour="text" predicate="not(preceding-sibling::node()[normalize-space() or self::*][1][self::fw])">
              <param name="content" value="' '"/>
            </model>
          </modelSequence>
          <model output="normalized" predicate="@break='no' or not(ancestor::titlePage)" behaviour="omit"/>
          <model output="plain" predicate="@break='no'" behaviour="omit">
            <param name="join" value="'-¬⸗&#xAD;&#x2010;&#x2011;'"/>
          </model>
          <model output="plain" behaviour="break">
            <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="note" mode="change">
          <!-- added: where the margin is, in the rendition of note-margin -->
          <model cssClass="note-speaker" predicate="@type='speaker'" behaviour="inline" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.72em; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <!-- printed beside or below the text, a Bible reference or a marginal note: never in the
               apparatus. `data-margin` puts it in the page's margin, on the printed side, where the
               window has room; otherwise it stays a small note in the line. -->
          <model cssClass="note-margin" predicate="@place='left' or @place='right' or @type='marginalia' or @type='bibl'" behaviour="inline" useSourceRendition="true">
            <param name="data-margin" value="if (@place='left') then 'left' else 'right'"/>
            <outputRendition>margin-inline: 0.3em; font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 1.3; color: rgb(var(--c-muted)); &amp; br { display: none; } @media (min-width: 58rem) { float: right; clear: right; width: 7rem; margin: 0.15em -7.5rem 0 0.5rem; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; &amp; br { display: inline; } &amp;[data-margin='left'] { float: left; clear: left; margin-inline: -7.5rem 0.5rem; text-align: right; } }</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model predicate="@type='remarkResponsibility'" behaviour="omit"/>
          <!-- a range comment: a numbered marker in the text, the note in the apparatus; the range
               runs from the anchor @targetEnd names to the marker -->
          <model cssClass="note-anchored" predicate="@targetEnd" behaviour="note" useSourceRendition="true">
            <param name="place" value="'end'"/>
            <param name="range" value="@targetEnd"/>
            <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.62em; font-weight: 600; vertical-align: super; line-height: 0; padding: 0 0.12em; color: rgb(var(--c-accent)); text-decoration: none; scroll-margin-top: 6rem;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <!-- a comment on the whole division: no marker, shown above the text; any other note is unmapped -->
          <model predicate="@type='annotation'" behaviour="note" useSourceRendition="true">
            <param name="place" value="'overview'"/>
          </model>
          <model output="plain" predicate="@targetEnd" behaviour="omit"/>
        </elementSpec>
      </schemaSpec>
    </body>
  </text>
</TEI>
